    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 34 tests pass with BUILD SUCCESS, including the new `Cp23Tests` (GOLD) and the existing `Cp15Tests` (SILVER/BRONZE).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the GOLD membership tier: an owner is GOLD when their household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) reaches 3+ members after their creation; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\nFollowing the same pattern as the existing `namesakeCount`, the household size is captured on the owner at creation time and used by the mapper that derives the tier at read time:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `householdSize` field (`household_size` column) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`AssignHouseholdSize.java`** (new function step) \u2014 after `AssignHousehold` stamps and back-fills the shared `householdId`, this counts owners with that same id plus the not-yet-persisted new owner, and stores the result. When the owner joined no household (`householdId == null`), size is 1.\n\n3. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `assignHouseholdSize` into the pipeline between `assignHousehold` and `assignCustomerCode`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `membershipTier` expression now returns `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise falls through to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE logic (so existing owners with a null size are unaffected).\n\n5. **Schemas/data** \u2014 added `household_size` to all four DB schemas (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) and appended the extra NULL to the positional owner inserts in the tested `hsqldb/data.sql`.\n\nOne note: `db/mysql/data.sql`'s positional owner inserts were already inconsistent with the column count before this change (9 values vs 11 columns) and that profile isn't exercised by the test suite, so I left its data rows as-is rather than mask a pre-existing discrepancy.",
